Language Machine 2
==================

Language Machine 2 is a Go port of the Language Machine. It exists because
of the original work, and the ideas, design and execution model that make it
worth porting are the original author's.

Original author
---------------

Peri Hankey <mpah@users.sourceforge.net>
  Designed and wrote the Language Machine (2005): the grammar and translator
  engine in which a rule applies when the expected and incoming symbol streams
  fail to match, the lmn notation, the lm-diagram, the bytecode, and the
  documentation and examples that this port is checked against.
  With thanks and respect for a remarkable body of work, generously released
  as free software.
  https://languagemachine.sourceforge.net

Language Machine 2
------------------

Mikhail Sorochan <msorc@users.sourceforge.net>
  Go port, tooling (lm, lmn2go) and ongoing maintenance.

